      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "If $\\frac{8x-12y}{4}$ is written in the form $ax+by,$ what are the values of $a$ and $b?$",
      "worked_solution": "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x-12y}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{8x}{4}-\\frac{12y}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{8}{4}\\cdot x-\\frac{12}{4}\\cdot y & = \\\\ 2x-3y & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above in the form $ax+by,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{(2)}_{⏟}}_{a}x+{{(-3)}_{⏟}}_{b}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$ and $b=-3.$",
